# The Picture in Picture window can be made as wide as its display (the maintainer's decision,
# 12 Nov; Arc stops at 61.7 % of the screen's width). Chromium keeps the window inside 80 % of the
# work area and cuts it down to that whenever the video's size changes, as a stream switching
# quality does. Here the window is made 95 % as wide as its display, the fixture's stream then
# doubles its size, and the window must still be 95 % as wide.
cra://open?url=file://${FIXTURES}/Pages/video.html
expect-log loaded file:
wait 2
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"document.getElementById('v').requestPictureInPicture().then(()=>'pip:open')","awaitPromise":true,"userGesture":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"pip:open"
wait 1
cra://debug?pipSize=0.95
expect-log pip: resized to
wait 1
cra://debug?pip=wide
expect-log Cra pip wide: windows=1 .* share=0.95 .* onScreen=1
cra://debug?cdp=Runtime.evaluate&params={"expression":"c.width=1280,c.height=720,'stream:'+c.width","returnByValue":true}
expect-log Cra cdp Runtime.evaluate .*"value":"stream:1280"
expect-log pip: Chromium cut
wait 2
cra://debug?pip=after
expect-log Cra pip after: windows=1 .* share=0.95 .* onScreen=1
